# tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_xaead_parity_witness.rish — Monocypher-source parity for XChaCha20-Poly1305, Monocypher's FLAGSHIP AEAD
# (crypto_aead_lock) — the 24-byte extended-nonce authenticated encryption Lotus's signed carry, Vault, and Comlink will actually reach for.
# Our authored crypto/xchacha20.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C (vendor/monocypher, CC0/BSD-dual), each compiled fresh and asked for
# their XChaCha20-Poly1305 ciphertext and tag over one published known-answer, diffed byte-for-byte. The SIXTH rung of the real Monocypher-
# source parity pattern — BLAKE2b opened it; X25519, Ed25519, the IETF-nonce AEAD, and Argon2 extended it; this rung closes the extended-nonce
# path the IETF AEAD rung did not exercise, exercising the HChaCha20 subkey derivation against the actual source. Season G · Cryptography.
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season G thread (Cryptography · Rye-native, Monocypher-parity, audit-ready).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md — Season G names the ChaCha/Poly line among the
# primitives to prove against the vendored Monocypher, and the AEAD as the composition that unblocks the Lotus signed carry. The IETF-nonce AEAD
# rung (tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_aead_parity_witness.rish) proved the inner RFC 8439 AEAD; this rung proves Monocypher's flagship crypto_aead_lock
# — the 24-byte-nonce XChaCha20-Poly1305 that HChaCha20-derives its subkey — which is the API a caller actually invokes.
# Kin: crypto/xchacha20.rye (our authored XChaCha20-Poly1305, GREEN against Zig's std.crypto and the published KAT) · crypto/aead.rye (the RFC
# 8439 AEAD it runs under the derived subkey) · crypto/chacha20.rye · crypto/poly1305.rye · tools/rye/monocypher_xaead_parity.rye (our printing
# harness) · tools/fixtures/monocypher_xaead_harness.c (Monocypher's printing harness) · tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_aead_parity_witness.rish (the
# IETF-nonce sibling). Monocypher stays the parity TARGET, vendored and unmodified, never a copied line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# THE PARITY: crypto_aead_lock is XChaCha20-Poly1305 (draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha §2.3) — subkey = HChaCha20(key, nonce[0..16]); subnonce =
# 0x00000000 ‖ nonce[16..24]; then the RFC 8439 ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD runs under (subkey, subnonce). That is exactly what crypto/xchacha20.rye
# composes. Each implementation prints two lines — the ciphertext and the tag — over the identical published inputs; the witness diffs the two
# outputs byte-for-byte AND anchors both to the published ciphertext and tag (Zig's std.crypto neutral test vector, mirrored in the xchacha20.rye
# selftest), so the oracle is a real second implementation, never a recited constant. Purely local — the key and nonce are a published test
# vector, no key of ours, no signature, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_monocypher_xaead_parity_witness.rish

say "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Language EN — Monocypher-source parity for XChaCha20-Poly1305, Monocypher's FLAGSHIP AEAD (crypto_aead_lock), the 24-byte extended-nonce authenticated encryption Lotus's signed carry, Vault, and Comlink will actually reach for. The IETF-nonce AEAD sibling proved the inner RFC 8439 AEAD; this rung proves our authored crypto/xchacha20.rye — which HChaCha20-derives a subkey from the whole 128-bit nonce prefix, then runs that AEAD — against the ACTUAL vendored Monocypher C over one published known-answer, byte-for-byte."
say "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Style Radiant — like against like. Our composed extended-nonce AEAD and the unmodified vendored Monocypher each compile fresh and each print, in order, the ciphertext (114 bytes) and the 16-byte Poly1305 tag over key 0x45x32, nonce 0x2ax24, associated data 'Additional data', and the RFC's own sunscreen plaintext. Two independent implementations, one draft-published construction; the parity is that the two outputs agree hex for hex, and that both agree with the published ciphertext and tag."
say "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Lens TAME — no fabricated constant is trusted: crypto_aead_lock is XChaCha20-Poly1305 (draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha §2.3), the same extended-nonce construction crypto/xchacha20.rye composes, and both outputs are anchored to a published known-answer. Monocypher is linked, never copied. Purely local — the key and nonce are a published test vector, no key of ours, no signature, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let cbin = "crypto/bin/monocypher_xaead"
let cout = "crypto/bin/monocypher_xaead.out"
let rout = "crypto/bin/rye_xaead.out"

# 1. Build the Monocypher C harness, linking the unmodified vendored source with zig cc.
let cbuild = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && ${zig} cc -O2 -I vendor/monocypher/src tools/fixtures/monocypher_xaead_harness.c vendor/monocypher/src/monocypher.c -o ${cbin}"]
assert cbuild.ok else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Monocypher C harness build failed — ${cbuild.err}"

# 2. Run the Monocypher C harness — two AEAD hex lines: ciphertext then tag.
let crun = run ["sh" "-c" "${cbin} > ${cout} 2>&1"]
assert crun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Monocypher C harness exited non-zero — see ${cout}"

# 3. Run our authored Rye harness — the same two AEAD hex lines over the identical inputs.
let rrun = run ["sh" "-c" "env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye run tools/rye/monocypher_xaead_parity.rye > ${rout} 2>&1"]
assert rrun.ok else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Rye harness exited non-zero — see ${rout}"

# 4. Byte-for-byte parity: the two two-line outputs must be identical.
let diff = run ["sh" "-c" "diff ${cout} ${rout} > /dev/null && echo same"]
assert (trim diff.out) == "same" else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: Monocypher and Rye XChaCha20-Poly1305 disagree — Monocypher:\n$(cat ${cout})\nRye:\n$(cat ${rout})"

# 5. Anchor to the world: the published ciphertext (line 1) and tag (line 2) — Zig's std.crypto neutral test vector, mirrored in the
#    crypto/xchacha20.rye selftest, an independent published anchor for the WHOLE extended-nonce construction, HChaCha20 subkey derivation included.
let kat_cipher = "994d2dd32333f48e53650c02c7a2abb8e018b0836d7175aec779f52e961780768f815c58f1aa52d211498db89b9216763f569c9433a6bbfcefb4d4a49387a4c5207fbb3b5a92b5941294df30588c6740d39dc16fa1f0e634f7246cf7cdcb978e44347d89381b7a74eb7084f754b90bde9aaf"
let kat_tag = "5a94b8f2a85efd0b50692ae2d425e234"

let got_cipher = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '1p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_cipher.out) == kat_cipher else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: ciphertext is not the published known-answer value"

let got_tag = run ["sh" "-c" "sed -n '2p' ${cout}"]
assert (trim got_tag.out) == kat_tag else "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: tag is not the published known-answer value"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${cout}"]
say "crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: the published XChaCha20-Poly1305 seal, agreed by both implementations (ciphertext then tag):\n${shown.out}"

say "GREEN crypto-monocypher-xaead-parity: our authored crypto/xchacha20.rye and the vendored Monocypher's own C, each compiled fresh, produce byte-for-byte identical XChaCha20-Poly1305 over one published known-answer — the ciphertext and the 16-byte tag both match, and both match the published values. The sixth real Monocypher-SOURCE parity rung, proving Monocypher's FLAGSHIP crypto_aead_lock: the extended-nonce path — HChaCha20 subkey derivation included — now meets the actual audit target byte-for-byte, closing the gap the IETF-nonce AEAD rung left. Monocypher stays vendored and unmodified, linked never copied. Purely local, no key of ours, no signature, no network, no funds, no device; constant-time timing-safety stays the named horizon."
